HASTE — ORBITING SPEED CHEVRONS
Still source image for frame 1 of a dynamic 12-frame loop

STATUS

This brief produced the current 12-frame HASTE orbiting-chevron animation.
The user approved the preview and integration. The generated frames have at
least 69 px of visible-content margin and no clipped edges.

REFERENCE IMAGE INPUT

No reference image is attached. Use only the established gold-and-turquoise
HASTE palette. Do not use the previous HASTE wind-trail or quickstep outputs as
visual references; this concept intentionally avoids long trails and abstract
swirls.

PROMPT

Create exactly one still 2D fantasy-game VFX sprite: the opening frame of a
fast loop of three orbiting magical speed chevrons behind a moving allied
unit. Render only the effect. The unit, its body, clothing, weapons, feet,
ground, terrain, projectiles, and battlefield must be absent; the game will
composite this transparent sprite behind a live unit.

Compose the effect around the empty space where the unit's torso would be.
Keep that central body area almost entirely transparent. For a unit moving
left to right, place all three glyphs on the rear (left) half of a compact,
invisible oval orbit: one large, bright glyph low and behind the unit, one
medium glyph near the middle of the rear arc, and one smaller, dimmer glyph
near the upper rear arc. Separate them clearly so each reads as its own shape.
The positions and brightness should suggest that the glyphs are circling the
unit, not forming a straight trail.

Each glyph is a bold, open, angular V-shaped mark like a simple `>` chevron,
built from two thick, slightly broken turquoise strokes with a restrained
warm-gold edge. Point the glyphs generally in the direction of travel. Make
their edges crisp and their silhouettes unmistakable when scaled down; use a
small, tight glow only on the brightest glyph. Keep the marks asymmetric and
magical rather than resembling text, a logo, a UI symbol, or road signage.

The renderer mirrors the effect for units facing the opposite direction, so
compose the source image with a clear left-to-right direction. Keep the
chevrons behind the future unit silhouette and mostly outside its central
torso area. The effect should communicate quick, controlled movement, not an
attack, impact, or damage state.

ANIMATION INTENT FOR A LATER GENERATION

- Move the three chevrons around a compact oval path on the rear half of the
  unit, with no camera movement and no movement of the gameplay anchor.
- Brighten each glyph in turn as it passes the lower-rear position, then let
  it dim while continuing around the arc.
- Keep all three glyphs separate and sharply defined; do not stretch them
  into trails or smear them with motion blur.
- Complete a seamless 12-frame loop with a brisk, even rhythm and no pause.

TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS

- Output exactly one PNG at 1024 x 576 pixels, landscape 16:9, RGBA with
  genuine alpha transparency.
- Use a fully transparent background, not a checkerboard or a dark/colored
  matte. Only the three chevrons and their restrained glow may contain visible
  pixels.
- Keep at least 64 px of transparent safety margin on every canvas edge; do
  not clip a glyph or its glow.
- Keep the central unit silhouette area mostly transparent. Use large, bold
  shapes and clean alpha edges that remain readable at battlefield scale.
- No animation, sprite sheet, alternate takes, contact sheet, or variations.
- Save the source as
  `assets_src/spells/haste/orbiting-chevrons-first-frame.png`.

NEGATIVE PROMPT

character, unit, person, face, body, clothing, feet, boot, shoe, footprint,
paw print, weapon, armor, fortress, catapult, projectile, battlefield,
ground, terrain, landscape, sky, scenery, opaque background, checkerboard,
flat background color, wind ribbon, wind trail, long streak, motion blur,
smear, spiral, swirl, ring, continuous circle, smoke, dense particles,
particle cloud, large bloom, cropped glyph, clipped glow, attack, impact,
explosion, fire, ice, lightning, damage, blood, team emblem, faction symbol,
text, letters, numbers, logo, UI, HUD, road sign, arrow icon, border, frame,
watermark, signature, photorealism, unrelated franchise, copied commercial
artwork

ACCEPTANCE CHECK

- The frame contains exactly three separate, bold, open chevron glyphs with a
  clear bright-to-dim sequence along a short rear-side arc.
- Their placement implies an orbit around an empty central unit area, not a
  straight trail, continuous ring, or static emblem.
- The shapes remain legible at small scale and are distinct from an attack or
  damage effect.
- The central body area stays mostly transparent, and the effect fits the
  fixed, mirrorable battlefield anchor.
- The background is genuinely transparent, with clean alpha edges and at
  least 64 px of clear margin on every edge.
